ubana GPVM Install Notes
========================

This checkout is intended for the MicroBooNE mcc9 `e17:prof` workflow
used to build and run `ubana/searchingforstrangeness` in a fresh MRB
development area on the GPVMs.


Fresh MRB Area
==============

Start from a clean GPVM shell, then enter the SL7 development container:

    /cvmfs/uboone.opensciencegrid.org/bin/shell_apptainer.sh

Inside the container, create and initialize a fresh MRB area:

    source /cvmfs/uboone.opensciencegrid.org/products/setup
    source /cvmfs/uboone.opensciencegrid.org/products/setup_uboone_mcc9.sh
    setup mrb

    export TOP=/exp/uboone/app/users/$USER/production/mcc9
    mkdir -p "$TOP"
    cd "$TOP"
    mrb newDev -q e17:prof
    source localProducts_*/setup


Source Checkouts
================

Clone the forked repositories under `srcs/`:

    cd "$TOP/srcs"
    git clone https://github.com/njlane314/ubana.git
    git clone https://github.com/njlane314/ubsim.git

The current `ubsim` fork `main` is pinned for the mcc9 stack and should
declare `geant4reweight v01_00_03e`, matching `uboonecode v08_00_00_82`.

Initialize the `searchingforstrangeness` submodule recorded by `ubana`:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubana"
    git submodule sync --recursive
    git submodule update --init --remote ubana/searchingforstrangeness

To inspect the recorded submodule revision:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubana/ubana/searchingforstrangeness"
    git rev-parse --short HEAD


Required Checks
===============

Before building, verify that the local `ubsim` checkout contains the
old-flux PPFX calculators required by the EventWeight FHiCLs:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubsim"
    grep -R -n 'UBOLDPPFX\|UBOLDPPFXCV' ubsim/EventWeight/Calculators

If that grep prints nothing, stop and fix the `ubsim` source before
building. A local build without those calculators will fail at runtime
when `ppfx_oldrw_cv` is requested.

Also verify that the local `ubsim` checkout is using the mcc9-compatible
geant4reweight dependency:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubsim"
    grep -n 'geant4reweight' ups/product_deps

The expected line is:

    geant4reweight        v01_00_03e

Update the top-level MRB package list after cloning by hand:

    cd "$TOP/srcs"
    mrb uc

After the first successful `mrbsetenv`, run `mrb uc` once more from
`$TOP/srcs` if needed so MRB can reorder the hand-added package blocks
correctly.  If `mrbsetenv` reports

    DIAGNOSTICS: there are no packages in .../srcs

then the usual fix is to return to `$TOP/srcs` and rerun:

    mrb uc


Build
=====

Re-establish the MRB environment from the top of the fresh area:

    cd "$TOP"
    source /cvmfs/uboone.opensciencegrid.org/products/setup
    source /cvmfs/uboone.opensciencegrid.org/products/setup_uboone_mcc9.sh
    setup mrb
    source localProducts_*/setup
    mrbsetenv

If re-sourcing the product stack in the same shell reports an `mrb`
version conflict such as `v4_05_01 vs v6_09_11`, prefer a fresh SL7
container shell before repeating the setup sequence.

Build from the analysis package checkout:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubana/ubana/searchingforstrangeness"
    source .build.sh

The helper script builds the MRB area and refreshes the runtime tarball.


Runtime Setup
=============

For local GPVM tests, use the package helper after a successful build:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubana/ubana/searchingforstrangeness"
    source .setup.sh

That script sets up the mcc9 products, restores the MRB environment
after `unsetup_all`, and prepends the local `ubana` and `ubsim`
installed runtime paths before falling back to CVMFS.


Local Smoke Test
================

Example local EventWeight test:

    cd "$TOP/srcs/ubana/ubana/searchingforstrangeness"
    SAM_DEF=prodgenie_numi_uboone_overlay_fhc_mcc9_run1_v28_v2_sample0 \
    OUTPUT_BASE_DIR="$PWD/out" \
    ./.local.sh dev/flux/run_stage_evtw_cv_dev.fcl 1

If this fails, check first:

  * `source .setup.sh` completed without MRB setup errors;
  * the local `ubsim` checkout includes `UBOLDPPFX` and `UBOLDPPFXCV`;
  * the `searchingforstrangeness` submodule is initialized at the
    revision recorded by `ubana`.


Batch Jobs
==========

Batch jobs use the tarball refreshed by `.build.sh`, so GPVM and job
submission testing should always be done from the same rebuilt MRB area.

After the local smoke test succeeds, submit only the EventWeight stage
first:

    project.py --xml xml/numi_reco2_run1_fhc_campaign.xml --stage beam_shard0_evtw --submit
    project.py --xml xml/numi_reco2_run1_fhc_campaign.xml --stage beam_shard0_evtw --check
